{"kind":"report","text":"Approve the complete generic MCP design at exact a8c6222f7566a42322ab54567ee40422e380bbf8, treee581f01d7227f659a716458d7017a777d5aa8a5e, under design request2c3832be / promise059afc only. The four user claims are supported by the proposed architecture and explicit witnesses. This accepts the design; W1–W7 and implementation acceptance remain work to perform.\n\nArchitecture: The server exposes dynamically derived acts for every inventory definition plus complete generic creation/read/preparation/record/send/wait/settlement/credential operations. Durable standalone roots and per-membership standing keep unfamiliar applications discoverable across connections and restarts. Native foreign-resource preparation steps retain independent answers and unknown recovery under one exact envelope, separate from final-act phase/receipt/settlement. Old pinned lanes stay callable after activation retirement. Whole-response continuations, whole-object exceptions and semantic catalog generations preserve content and avoid needless observation-head invalidation. Default, generic replacement and add modes have explicit recipes. No per-application execution code or obsolete fixed tool-count constraint is imposed.\n\nNaming repair: Full native definition name, kind and declaration form binding identity. Names are mapped first, then resolved globally; collisions give every identity a deterministic variant, including identical ActType rows with different native routing. No platform alias is privileged. Native register.found and genesis install, field type scope and CLI acts/log are preserved beneath room.create/create/inspect/record surface names. Words never rewrite signed kinds, fields/types, target/incarnation, expected revision, beside domains or meaning. Native custody identity is independent of editable words; the words digest changes semantic discovery. All continuation pointers use inspect with describe. The three28ff4ada corrections are satisfied.\n\nSecur